CHECK mode == "generate"

DO Read ../../references/be-human.md once and ../../references/technical-summary.md#summary-content for writing.

DO Inspect branch/HEAD before reusing earlier code evidence. Resolve the requested
    implementation scope; retain Boolean scope_is_clear. Wording edits need no code
    investigation.

IF scope_is_clear == FALSE:
    ASK "Which changes or commit range should this technical summary cover?" AS summary_scope

    DO Resolve scope from summary_scope; update scope_is_clear.

    CHECK scope_is_clear == TRUE

DO Review relevant local changes or the explicitly identified commit range within the
    resolved scope. For wording edits, use existing evidence without code investigation.
    Follow exact imports or symbols only for material gaps. No PR target, fetch, clean-tree
    gate, commits, or tests solely to write prose. Distinguish observed checks from proposed
    verification and report incomplete implementation honestly.

DO Prepare in-memory draft using the shared Summary content rules. For a new file, use
    a # TICKET-ID heading followed by the Description body from ../../assets/pr.md, without the PR
    title or Description heading. For existing files, preserve layout, accurate developer notes,
    and unrequested content; generate must not reset an existing summary.

CHECK Requested content in draft is supported and complete, with no placeholders in changed
    fields. Preserve accurate developer judgments and report unrelated incomplete fields.

DO Recheck ticket.md's active ID as current_ticket_id.

CHECK current_ticket_id == ticket_id

DO Save draft only to summary_path, then verify the saved file once against draft.

PRINT with summary_path, material uncertainty, and unrelated gaps, briefly.
